&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Formlabs:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Do you want to change how the world creates?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Formlabs, we’re building the tools that make it possible for anyone to bring their ideas to life, from cutting-edge products to life-saving medical devices. Our 3D printing technology powers innovation at more than 50,000 industry leaders worldwide, including Apple, Google, Tesla, New Balance, and NASA. Together, we’re helping everyone design, prototype, and manufacture faster than ever before.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a team of hands-on builders, engineers, and innovators reinventing how the world makes physical things. If you’re ready to shape the future of fabrication, come build it with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Formlabs is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Finance &amp;amp; Operations Staff &lt;/strong&gt;to bridge our transactional finance operations and physical plant production. This role is designed for a systems-minded, highly organized professional who thrives at the intersection of accounting, data analysis, and manufacturing operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you will spend your time maintaining foundational transactional accuracy and driving inventory control, Bill of Materials maintenance (“BOM”), and workflow optimization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Accounts Payable &amp;amp; Employee Expenses&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High-Speed Transactional Processing:&lt;/strong&gt; Accurately process vendor invoices, credit notes, and employee Travel &amp;amp; Expense (T&amp;amp;E) reimbursement claims.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dispute &amp;amp; Inquiry Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the primary point of contact for vendor inquiries, reconciling outstanding balances and resolving processing blocks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Inventory Production Data Entry &amp;amp; Integrity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Daily Performance Logging:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with the plant production team to gather and input daily manufacturing data including the material consumptions, general inventory adjustments into the ERP systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production Sheet Integrity:&lt;/strong&gt; Audit daily logs for discrepancies, missing records, or timing lags to ensure the team is working with 100% accurate plant-floor data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Inventory Management, Costing &amp;amp; BOM Maintenance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BOM &amp;amp; Cost Maintenance:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the maintenance of accurate Bills of Materials (BOMs) and item costs in the ERP, flagging structural discrepancies between planned and actual configurations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical &amp;amp; Systemic Inventory Audits:&lt;/strong&gt; Coordinate periodically inventory reconciliations, and research inventory counting variances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Process Optimization &amp;amp; Analytical Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Improvement Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Actively look for small, daily efficiencies. Partner with leadership to identify manual bottlenecks on both the accounting and plant sides.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Reporting &amp;amp; SOPs:&lt;/strong&gt; Assist managers by pulling and formatting variance reports to provide leadership with the clean data needed to make strategic decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are energized by both office finance work and factory-floor operations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy working across teams (from accounting managers to production line workers) to close process loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are highly receptive to feedback, eager to learn, and open-minded.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy learning how software applications integrate. You want to understand how data flows between Coupa, NetSuite,etc..&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience resolving transactional discrepancies in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Supply Chain, Business Administration, or related field is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 2–4 years of experience in plant manufacturing environment with key focus on accounts payable, inventory management, cost accounting, and data analysis,.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems Exposure:&lt;/strong&gt; Direct experience using mid-to-enterprise ERP platforms (e.g., NetSuite, SAP, Hyperion HFM or QAD) and modern procurement databases (Concur or Coupa) is highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BOM &amp;amp; Inventory Literacy:&lt;/strong&gt; Solid foundational understanding of inventories, Bill of Materials configurations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excel / Google Sheets Proficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Intermediate spreadsheet skills (XLOOKUP, VLOOKUP, Pivot Tables) to easily clean and analyze production databases and support management reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Benefits &amp;amp; Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, Dental, Vision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3% match of yearly salary for 401(k)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EAP Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-office catering 3x per week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;120 hours of PTO per year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and value diversity at our company.&amp;nbsp; We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Even if you don&#39;t check every box, but see yourself contributing, please apply.&lt;/strong&gt; Help us build an inclusive community that will change the face of 3D printing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Join Formlabs if you want to bring ground-breaking professional 3D printers to the desktop of every designer, engineer, researcher, and artist in the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Finance Systems team owns the enterprise systems used to record, process, and report financial data across Formlabs. We&#39;re looking for a Finance Systems Engineer who is equally comfortable writing code to automate and interconnect our finance stack and administering those systems day-to-day — owning the configuration, access, and operational health that keep NetSuite and Coupa running as a compliant, efficient source of truth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role for someone who wants to both build (scripting, integrations, automation) and operate (privileged administration, BaU configuration, security). If you&#39;re as happy shipping a SuiteScript integration as you are provisioning a role, tuning an approval workflow, or debugging a failed PO sync, this is the role for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build &amp;amp; Integrate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, and ship customizations and integrations across &lt;strong&gt;NetSuite, Coupa, and related financial systems (such as Adaptive, Avalara, or future custom-built tools)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain integrations between finance systems and the wider landscape-&amp;nbsp; Shopify, Salesforce, the data warehouse, and middleware/iPaaS — using REST/SOAP APIs, webhooks, and event-driven patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate reconciliations, data syncs, and reporting pipelines so that procurement, invoicing, sales, GL, and revenue data flow accurately across platforms in near real time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write SQL and saved searches to power reporting that pulls from multiple sources and aligns with finance and business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply modern engineering practices- version control, code review, testing, and clear documentation-&amp;nbsp; to deliver maintainable, well-documented solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Administer &amp;amp; Operate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a &lt;strong&gt;privileged administrator&lt;/strong&gt; for NetSuite and Coupa, owning day-to-day system health, configuration, and change management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage user provisioning and deprovisioning, roles, permissions, and periodic access/security reviews to enforce least-privilege and support audit and audit and internal controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and maintain custom fields, records, forms, workflows, approval routing, and notifications as business processes evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own saved searches, reports, dashboards, and KPIs; keep the reporting layer accurate and self-serve for finance stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Procurement approval chains and limits, content and account groups, supplier onboarding/SIM, and PO/invoice/expense configuration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage sandbox refreshes, release-preview and version testing, feature enablement, and bundle/SuiteApp management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support period closes by maintaining subsidiary, tax, and entity configuration, and by monitoring integration error queues, audit logs, and data integrity across systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own license and subscription management, and act as the first line of triage for system issues, partnering with vendors and internal teams to resolve them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A university degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in finance systems engineering, ERP administration, or systems integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on, demonstrable experience with &lt;strong&gt;NetSuite&lt;/strong&gt; (both SuiteScript development &lt;em&gt;and&lt;/em&gt; administration) and &lt;strong&gt;Coupa&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage system integrations using APIs and/or middleware tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to write SQL from scratch and comfort with reporting and data-warehouse concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of finance, procurement, and accounting workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A pragmatic problem-solver with excellent communication skills, willing to wear many hats and jump in wherever needed to deliver outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NetSuite certifications (SuiteFoundation, Administrator, or SuiteScript Developer) and/or Coupa administration experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with additional finance/business systems (Salesforce, Shopify, Avalara/AvaTax, or similar) and iPaaS middleware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to effectively leverage AI coding and tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a fast-paced, high-growth company that manufactures and sells physical products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Perks &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Robust equity program to build future wealth through RSUs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive healthcare coverage (Medical, Dental, Vision)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Low cost fund options in our 401K and access to advisors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid Parental Leave (up to 16 weeks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tenure-based paid Sabbatical Leave (up to 6 weeks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Out of Office Plan – Take time when you need it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ample free on-site parking &amp;amp; pre-tax commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthy on-site lunches, snacks, beverages, &amp;amp; treats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular sponsored professional development opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Many opt-in culture events across our diverse community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;And of course… unlimited 3D prints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Equity is a big part of the compensation package at Formlabs - every employee receives equity because everyone contributes to building the company. We have a lot of confidence in the products we’re building and the impact we’re making, and you should too.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay is the other part of our compensation package, and it is carefully determined based on your skills, experience, and expected impact. Equity and base pay combine to make up your total compensation package at Formlabs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual base pay range for this role is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$105,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$140,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

