&lt;p&gt;Join Formlabs if you want to bring ground-breaking professional 3D printers to the desktop of every designer, engineer, researcher, and artist in the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the &lt;strong&gt;Head of Information Technology (IT) &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;at Formlabs, you will own the foundation the whole company runs on: our global network, on-premise servers, endpoints, IT service desk, identity and access, and the security program that protects Formlabs and our customers’ data. This is a single, combined leadership role — where you will lead as a player-coach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead a global team of 7 spanning network administration, systems administration, help desk, and cybersecurity, and support offices in Somerville, Germany, Budapest, and Shenzhen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join the Systems team, which enables every Formlabs team with enterprise applications, infrastructure, data, AI, and security. You will report to the CIO.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in our Somerville, MA office and is an onsite role.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Job:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead, coach, and develop a team of 7 across network, systems, help desk, and cybersecurity. Set clear priorities, build strong technical leadership within the team, and grow the team’s automation and scripting skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Network &amp;amp; Connectivity:&lt;/strong&gt; Own our Cisco Meraki estate across four countries — SD-WAN and site-to-site VPN, firewalls, segmentation, Wi-Fi, ISP circuits, cloud VPN tunnels, remote access, and the specific connectivity and compliance requirements of operating in China.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy &amp;amp; Roadmap:&lt;/strong&gt; Define and drive a combined infrastructure and security roadmap that balances reliability, risk, cost, and user experience — and explain it in business terms to the CIO, CFO, and company leadership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Servers &amp;amp; Resilience:&lt;/strong&gt; Own on-premise compute (Proxmox) and the services that run on it — lifecycle, patching, monitoring, backup and tested restores, and disaster recovery — and make deliberate decisions about what stays on-prem versus moves to cloud or SaaS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security Program:&lt;/strong&gt; Own Formlabs’ cybersecurity program end to end: policy, risk register, vulnerability and patch management, endpoint protection, email and SaaS security, logging, data loss prevention, and incident detection, response runbooks, and exercises.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Staffing Model &amp;amp; Services:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide leadership on how the team is staffed and which services it relies on — deciding what to build in-house versus source from managed service and security partners — and hold those partners accountable to clear scope and SLAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identity &amp;amp; Access:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the joiner/mover/leaver process, SSO and MFA, privileged and break-glass access, and admin hygiene across Google Workspace and core SaaS — with the evidence trail auditors expect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IT Service Desk &amp;amp; Endpoints:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure a fast, friendly, measurable help desk for ~800 employees — ticket SLAs, onboarding/offboarding, laptop lifecycle and MDM, conference room and A/V, and site support — and personally own the hardest escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation &amp;amp; AI:&lt;/strong&gt; Replace manual, repeatable work with automation and AI-assisted workflows across provisioning, monitoring, ticket triage, and reporting, so the team scales with the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendors &amp;amp; Budget:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the infrastructure and security vendor portfolio and budget — contracts, renewals, licensing, and hardware refresh plans — and make clear build/buy/partner tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation &amp;amp; Continuity:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain current diagrams, inventories, runbooks, and on-call/escalation coverage so no system depends on a single person’s knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 8+ years in IT infrastructure and/or security, including 2+ years leading teams, ideally in a mid-sized (500–2,000 person) company with multiple international sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Network &amp;amp; Systems Depth:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on expertise in enterprise networking (routing, VPN, firewalls, segmentation, Wi-Fi) and server virtualization; you can review a firewall rule set or a backup design yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Practical experience building or running a security program at a company without a large dedicated security team — including EDR, identity, vulnerability management, and incident response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Service Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; You care how employees experience IT, measure service quality, and lead a help desk with the same rigor as a network.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to design a team’s staffing and sourcing model, and to select, negotiate with, and hold managed service providers accountable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Translate technical risk into clear business decisions for executives, and write clear policies, runbooks, and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Controls &amp;amp; Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with frameworks such as NIST CSF, ISO 27001, or SOC 2, and with IT general controls in an audit-ready environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a technical field or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Cisco Meraki, Proxmox, CrowdStrike, Google Workspace, and Cloudflare.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating IT in China (cross-border connectivity, local regulations, remote-site support).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with GCP and AWS security fundamentals (IAM, logging, network controls).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scripting/automation skills (Python, PowerShell, Terraform, or similar) and hands-on use of AI tools in IT or security operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security certifications such as CISSP, CISM, or CCNP Security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a hardware or manufacturing company with R&amp;amp;D labs and lab networks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
