&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Formlabs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To reinvent an industry, you have to build the best team. Join Formlabs if you want to bring ground-breaking professional 3D printers to the desktop of every designer, engineer, researcher, manufacturer, and artist in the world. Formlabs manufacturing operations are the key to placing powerful digital fabrication tools into the hands of designers and engineers around the world. Manufacturing thousands of printers is already an enormous task – and the complexity will grow as we build tens and even hundreds of thousands of electronic products each year.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Operations Program Manager (OPM) will play a critical role in scaling the production of Formlabs&#39; 3D printers and ensuring smooth and efficient manufacturing operations in the Shenzhen Bay area. You will be a key leader in new product introduction (NPI), managing the entire lifecycle from concept to mass production. This role requires close collaboration with cross-functional teams in engineering, supply chain, quality, and production, both internally and with our manufacturing partners.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead NPI programs for new 3D printers and accessories, ensuring successful product launches that meet quality, cost, and delivery targets.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute comprehensive manufacturing plans, including capacity planning, production scheduling, and materials management.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with engineering teams to ensure Design for Manufacturing (DFM) principles are implemented and to resolve any production challenges.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with contract manufacturers and other key suppliers in the region, ensuring adherence to quality standards and production schedules.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and implement process improvements to optimize production efficiency, reduce costs, and enhance product quality.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively manage risks and issues, developing mitigation plans and escalating concerns as needed.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate program status and updates to key organizational stakeholders, including executive leadership.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Engineering or a related field. MBA is considered a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in operations program management, preferably in the consumer electronics or high-tech manufacturing industry.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Results-oriented and attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of successfully launching new products into mass production.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of manufacturing processes, quality control systems, and supply chain management.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build relationships and influence stakeholders at all levels.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Lean manufacturing principles and Six Sigma methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English and Mandarin Chinese.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 40%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Do you want to change how the world creates?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Formlabs, we’re building the tools that make it possible for anyone to bring their ideas to life, from cutting-edge products to life-saving medical devices. Our 3D printing technology powers innovation at more than 50,000 industry leaders worldwide, including Apple, Google, Tesla, New Balance, and NASA. Together, we’re helping everyone design, prototype, and manufacture faster than ever before.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a team of hands-on builders, engineers, and innovators reinventing how the world makes physical things. If you’re ready to shape the future of fabrication, come build it with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Global Operations team makes sure that our products can be enjoyed by thousands of people around the world. If you have a passion for operations, data, problem-solving, and working in a fast-paced environment, we want you to join us as our&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Operations Systems Analyst, Netsuite &lt;/strong&gt;. Your role will be to further develop our systems ensuring a positive customer order Fulfillment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are the change-enabler for the Customer Fulfillment team and its dedicated technical partner. You own our operations NetSuite capabilities, automate manual processes, define requirements for new tools, and implement them into our daily workflows so the team can scale sustainably.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take a growing role in our warehouse integrations, working with our systems team to keep data flowing cleanly between NetSuite, Shopify, and our 3PL partners. You help identify and resolve discrepancies between physical 3PL stock and system inventory records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You own key fulfillment dashboards in Looker, including inventory and lead time reporting. This means managing them day to day and rebuilding them on more robust, automated foundations as our needs grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You help move the team from manual reporting to live, automated tracking of performance metrics like order-to-delivery time and on-time delivery, pulling together data from BigQuery, NetSuite, and carrier sources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You execute projects from our global roadmap and bring your own ideas for improvement. You represent Customer Fulfillment in wider systems meetings and solution design projects, translating our needs into clear requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work closely with the global Customer Fulfillment team, the wider Global Operations team, technical systems teams, and company leadership.&amp;nbsp; The role has real room to grow and can be shaped around your strengths and interests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 to 3 years of experience in operations systems, business systems, or a similar technical role, with a Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related engineering field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NetSuite Admin Certification and experience across Warehouse Management, Inventory, Procurement &amp;amp; Supply Chain, and Finance &amp;amp; Accounting. You can build and optimize workflows, saved searches, and reports, and implement scripts as well as make modifications to the ERP production infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SQL skills, ideally in BigQuery, including connecting BigQuery to Google Sheets to deliver reporting. Basic proficiency in Python and/or JavaScript, plus strong Google Workspace and Excel skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the EDI messages exchanged between ERP, WMS, and 3PL systems (e.g., purchase orders, ASNs, shipment confirmations, inventory advice) and have supported system integrations while maintaining high standards for data integrity.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
