&lt;p&gt;At Formlabs, we’re building 3D printers that are changing the way things get made. We have the smartest minds across every engineering discipline, and the technology they’re building is deployed at more than 50,000 industry leaders worldwide, including Apple, Google, Tesla, New Balance, and NASA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Formlabs products span many technical areas including electronics, motion control, sensing technologies, machine vision, optics, material science, embedded firmware, and PC software. These technologies must all work in concert with each other in order to ship world class products. The System Integration team is the glue that binds the systems together; from making the first prototypes function to the final error handling code that keeps the products reliable.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the &lt;strong&gt;Robotic Systems Integration Engineering Manager&lt;/strong&gt;, you will lead a high performance team of mutli-disciplenary engineers. You and your team will be responsible for defining and integrating sensors and actuators, bringing up and maintaining prototype fleets, developing algorithms and control systems, and delivering embedded firmware for physical systems across the entire Formlabs product portfolio.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the System Integration team by example; take a hands-on approach to technology development by balancing customer value, cost, and engineering effort to consistently deploy optimal solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead high level architecture decision making around sensing technologies, actuators, control algorithms, calibration techniques, and firmware architecture across all Formlabs products&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research external products and new technologies to ensure Formlabs products continue to use state of the art algorithms and sensing technologies.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy resources across programs, prioritize assignments, and hire top level engineers to build a balanced and dynamic team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are an expert in control algorithms, sensors, actuators, and embedded systems for complex, high precision products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can lead and grow a high performance engineering team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a history of developing successful products in a fast paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are a hands-on contributor actively involved in the daily activities and technical decisions of your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a refined instinct for balancing performance with complexity. You are always thinking about what work to do, and more importantly, what work not to do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
