&lt;p&gt;As a Strategy &amp;amp; Operations Analyst&amp;nbsp;at Formlabs, you will turn messy business problems into shipped solutions. You’ll take problem statements from teams across the company — Finance, Operations, Sales, Support, R&amp;amp;D — scope them, rally the right people, and build much of the solution yourself with SQL, Python, automation, and AI tools. You’ll also be a key partner to the CIO in running the IT &amp;amp; Systems organization: driving OKRs, reporting, and roadmapping across a 26-person team spanning data platform, digital systems, financial systems, infrastructure, and cybersecurity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for someone early in their career with a very strong ability to learn quickly — someone who has done analytical or operations work at a consulting firm, startup, or BizOps team, and who would rather build the fix than write the deck about it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report directly to the CIO and work closely with the leaders of each IT &amp;amp; Systems team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in our Somerville, MA office and will be a hybrid role with the expectation of at least 3 days a week in office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Job:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Problem Delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; Take ambiguous problem statements from the business, define requirements and success measures, and lead small cross-functional teams from scoping through launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-On Building:&lt;/strong&gt; Write the SQL queries, Python scripts, integrations, and low-code or AI-powered automations that close gaps between systems — then hand off steady-state ownership to the right domain team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OKRs &amp;amp; Planning:&lt;/strong&gt; Run the IT &amp;amp; Systems OKR process — gather inputs, track progress, and surface risks early so leadership can make decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting &amp;amp; Roadmaps:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the data, cadence, and first draft of recurring leadership reporting, roadmap rollups, and spend reporting (cloud, SaaS, and AI tools).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Improve how the organization runs — software purchasing, renewals, license hygiene, and vendor coordination — with a bias toward automating the process rather than doing it by hand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Prepare analysis and materials for executive and cross-functional discussions, translating technical work into business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
