&lt;p&gt;Do you want to change how the world creates?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At &lt;strong&gt;Formlabs&lt;/strong&gt;, we’re building the tools that make it possible for anyone to bring their ideas to life, from cutting-edge products to life-saving medical devices. Our 3D printing technology powers innovation at more than 50,000 industry leaders worldwide, including &lt;strong&gt;Apple, Google, Tesla, New Balance, and NASA&lt;/strong&gt;. Together, we’re helping everyone design, prototype, and manufacture faster than ever before.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you will help building and shipping &lt;a href=&quot;https://formlabs.com/eu/software/#preform&quot;&gt;PreForm&lt;/a&gt;, own PreForm&#39;s quality and performance signal - make quality automated, measurable, and enforced at the PR gate. We’re a team of hands-on builders, engineers, and innovators reinventing how the world makes physical things. If you’re ready to shape the future of fabrication, come build it with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Job:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance regression detection.&lt;/strong&gt; Per-PR and nightly measurement of the defined KPIs (startup, upload, print generation, crash rate) in CI, with alerting on regression. This is the enforcement mechanism for the PreForm performance initiative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systemtest re-architecture on the PreForm Local API.&lt;/strong&gt; Rebuild the systemtest layer to drive end-to-end scenarios headlessly through PreForm Server, in alignment with the API team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer-file corpus testing.&lt;/strong&gt; Build and own a pipeline that runs large batches of real customer models through slicing and support generation and diffs results against baselines - catching regressions on the geometry customers actually print, at a scale manual testing cannot reach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Crash intelligence.&lt;/strong&gt; Own Sentry triage, trending, and root-cause attribution; build crash-reproduction harnesses so engineers fix rather than investigate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test infrastructure stewardship.&lt;/strong&gt; Print regression baselines, CI flake, test runtimes, golden-file management - owned as a product instead of taxing feature engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;C++ proficiency.&lt;/strong&gt; Able to write integration and system tests against PreForm internals and understand what they exercise (mesh operations, print file generation, slicing output). Not necessarily a geometry expert; not afraid of the codebase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Python for tooling and harnesses.&lt;/strong&gt; Corpus pipelines, API-driven test drivers, result diffing and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CI and automation depth.&lt;/strong&gt; Jenkins, test parallelization, flake management, baseline/golden-file testing strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Observability instinct.&lt;/strong&gt; Sentry, Amplitude, crash and performance dashboards. Treats &#39;is this release healthy&#39; as a data question.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desktop application testing experience (strong plus).&lt;/strong&gt; GUI automation on Windows/macOS (Squish or Qt Test-based harnesses)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Seniority: mid-to-senior IC.&lt;/strong&gt; Senior enough to define the test strategy independently; hands-on enough to build it. Real IC appetite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
