&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Trade Show Specialist&lt;/strong&gt; is based at our largest European office, in Budapest. This role works closely with Sales, Marketing, Product, Design and Leadership to shape how Formlabs shows up on some of our most important stages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role owns the strategy, planning, execution, and performance of a portfolio of events, with a strong focus on key trade shows and Formlabs-owned events. Formlabs participates in approximately 20 trade shows annually, ranging from smaller, 12sqm booths to large-format exhibits of over 200sqm, while continuously bringing new products and applications to market. You will independently define and execute event programs, collaborate across functions to achieve clear objectives, and continuously improve how our experiential marketing efforts support the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Job:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a portfolio of various trade shows, from 12sqm to 200+sqm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute plans to achieve event objectives, ensuring milestones are met and outcomes are delivered&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end event planning and execution, including pre/post-event campaigns, staffing, booth management, and internal enablement for demos and presentations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the design and marketing teams to ensure event presence effectively represents the brand and showcases our growing product portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage budgets, contracts, vendors, and logistics, optimizing spend and operational efficiency across multiple event formats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a visible brand ambassador, building relationships with customers, partners, and prospects onsite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather and analyze event performance insights, using learnings to continuously improve formats, messaging, and attendee experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across Sales, Product, Design, and Marketing teams, providing recommendations and influencing decisions to maximize event impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for ordering and tracking event inventory including collateral, giveaways, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel as needed (~25% of the time) to attend events, oversee execution, and support onsite teams - mostly within Europe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
